WEBVTT

00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:08.792
I asked her if we'd met before.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:12.542
She said, "Don't you think
this flirting style is a bit outdated?"

00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:16.792
I said, "No, I genuinely
feel like we've met before."

00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:18.667
So, she took a tissue

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.708
and gave a mischievous, childlike smile.

00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:22.250
Exactly like yours.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.375
With exactly that kind of smile,

00:00:24.458 --> 00:00:26.292
she said, "Maybe we have."

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:30.458
I said, "I can't remember where we met.
If you do, tell me."

00:00:31.292 --> 00:00:34.667
She said, "Maybe we met in a book."

00:00:35.208 --> 00:00:39.417
I said, "Oh, come on! Isn't
this flirting style a bit too fresh?"

00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:42.417
Chander Mohan Sharma?
Hey, I'm Kushal--

00:00:43.208 --> 00:00:46.333
I'm Kushal. We met with Sudha
in Bhopal, remember?

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:48.292
Oh!

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.667
How did you recognize me?

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.917
How could I forget?

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.750
That was my first official date
with my wife, Priya.

00:00:57.292 --> 00:00:58.208
Hi.

00:00:58.292 --> 00:00:59.917
We're here on our anniversary trip.

00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:02.417
Happy anniversary.

00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:06.875
How is Sudha? Is she here with you?

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.000
- Hey, C.
- Yeah.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:13.208
Divya Prakash would like you
to say a few words.

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:15.250
- You do it, please.
- Okay.

00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:17.333
Listen, Preeti. That's…

00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:19.625
- Kushal.
- Kushal.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.167
Hi.

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.625
Preeti, my partner.

00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:27.750
Man, is this your cafe?

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:30.667
What a beautiful space
you've put together!

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:31.625
Thanks.

00:01:32.542 --> 00:01:33.792
Alright, see you later.

00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:36.750
See you. If there's anything you need,
please let me know.

00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:38.625
Yeah? Take care.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.583
I said, "Let me read the whole thing."

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:46.375
It went on to say that no story is a lie.

00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:48.708
Each one has either already happened,

00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:50.917
is happening,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.167
or is yet to unfold.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.500
{\an8}MOM: I'M COMING TOMORROW MORNING
BY BHOPAL EXPRESS. I WILL ARRIVE BY 6:30

00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:43.333
{\an8}Sudha.

00:02:44.375 --> 00:02:47.500
{\an8}Sudha, wake up!
Wake up and see this.

00:02:57.125 --> 00:02:58.208
- Now what?
- Now what?

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:06.833
- Here.
- Thank you.

00:03:15.625 --> 00:03:16.708
Why are you laughing?

00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:18.292
Give me a hand.

00:03:18.375 --> 00:03:20.250
- Five more minutes, then I'll be out.
- Okay.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.667
- Come on!
- Listen. Where will you go?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.500
To Gargi's. Where else?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Wait a minute. Wait.

00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:31.792
I… I can't believe
we're doing all of this.

00:03:32.458 --> 00:03:36.417
We're behaving like college kids
who've been caught stealing.

00:03:38.708 --> 00:03:42.875
Okay, how about I just say
you're a colleague's relative?

00:03:44.042 --> 00:03:48.125
Or their friend, or their sister,
who has come here for some work--

00:03:48.208 --> 00:03:50.208
Don't even think about lying.

00:03:50.292 --> 00:03:51.333
You'll get caught.

00:03:51.917 --> 00:03:53.417
So, should I tell the truth?

00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:56.292
I dare you, Chander Mohan Sharma.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.292
- Yes, Aunty.
- Its wheel keeps coming off.

00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:02.167
You've gotten very weak
after getting married.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.500
You should eat some <i>sattu.</i>

00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:05.667
- Come on, give it to me.
- I'll manage, Aunty. Go ahead.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.500
You'll manage? Manage yourself first!

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:14.417
Mom! You?

00:04:15.042 --> 00:04:17.167
I sent you a text saying I was coming.

00:04:17.792 --> 00:04:20.833
- So early?
- The train arrived early. Come on.

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:23.542
- Mom!
- Ugh, you haven't bathed!

00:04:27.792 --> 00:04:30.458
This is Sudha, Mom.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.958
She's my friend's sister.

00:04:33.042 --> 00:04:34.708
Just visiting.

00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:39.000
Did you go to Chander's university too?

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.750
No, I spilled coffee on myself.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.708
- Alright then. Chander, I'll leave.
- Yeah, yeah, bye!

00:04:49.792 --> 00:04:51.500
- Yeah, okay.
- Hey, wait.

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:54.083
- Come on. No, no.
- No, Aunty, I'll take it.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.083
I'll take it, dear. Come.

00:04:59.042 --> 00:05:01.167
Didn't you catch up on your sleep today?

00:05:04.917 --> 00:05:06.125
It's my mother!

00:05:11.708 --> 00:05:13.250
So, Sudha, what do you do?

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:15.333
She's a law student, Mom. Final year.

00:05:16.042 --> 00:05:17.625
Is your name Sudha?

00:05:20.792 --> 00:05:21.792
Yes, Aunty.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.458
I'll always be a law student.

00:05:24.542 --> 00:05:25.750
But now, I'm a lawyer.

00:05:26.417 --> 00:05:28.167
I practice right here in Bhopal.

00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:30.417
So, since when…

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:33.500
It's been about a month.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.417
Is this the same Sudha?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.375
Sudha Tripathi, whom I introduced you to

00:05:45.458 --> 00:05:47.000
a few months ago?

00:05:47.708 --> 00:05:49.500
Dear, does your mom live in Ratlam?

00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:51.208
Yes, Aunty.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
Good morning, <i>bhaiya!</i>

00:05:56.083 --> 00:05:57.333
Good morning, <i>didi!</i>

00:05:57.417 --> 00:06:00.417
I bought eggs for you both-- Aunty!

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.667
When did you arrive?

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.750
You bought eggs for them.

00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:11.333
I'll go make some tea for you.

00:06:14.292 --> 00:06:17.333
- Aunty, I'm sorry, but I have to go now.
- No, that's okay.

00:06:17.417 --> 00:06:18.458
Nice meeting you.

00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:20.625
- Take care of yourself.
- I will.

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:26.417
I'm so sorry.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.708
I'll wait downstairs.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.583
Didn't you reject this match?

00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:42.750
Mom, I need to go to the office. I have
a very important presentation today.

00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:44.000
We can sit and talk this evening.

00:06:44.083 --> 00:06:46.292
Have tea and take some rest.
You must be tired.

00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:47.250
Bye.

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:51.250
A colleague's sister? Really?

00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:53.792
I got really nervous, Sudha.
I'm really very sorry.

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:55.167
Yeah, but what was that?

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.583
That was my mom!

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.333
I said I'm sorry.

00:06:58.917 --> 00:07:00.958
This right here is a core memory.

00:07:01.042 --> 00:07:04.083
That's not a core memory, that's trauma!

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.583
Hold this.

00:07:07.667 --> 00:07:09.833
- I'll take it.
- No, you open the gate.

00:07:13.083 --> 00:07:15.750
- Why didn't you tell the truth?
- What should I have said?

00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:18.875
"Mom, this is Sudha,
my live-in girlfriend,

00:07:18.958 --> 00:07:22.542
who suddenly booked tickets
to the Andaman Islands last night

00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:24.792
so we could go celebrate our honeymoon

00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:26.708
because she doesn't want to get married."

00:07:26.792 --> 00:07:28.000
Should I have said that?

00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:31.000
When did I say I was your girlfriend?

00:07:32.917 --> 00:07:34.167
So, what should I have said?

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:37.250
You should have said,
"Mom, this is Sudha."

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:39.833
"She only wants three things from men."

00:07:40.417 --> 00:07:42.708
"Lust, lust, and lust."

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.708
What even are you?

00:07:46.375 --> 00:07:48.375
Come on, I'll drop you off at Gargi's.

00:07:48.458 --> 00:07:50.208
No. I'll go myself.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.792
Meet me tonight. We'll strategize.

00:07:54.333 --> 00:07:55.333
My lunchbox.

00:07:57.292 --> 00:07:58.458
- Bye.
- Bye.

00:08:06.542 --> 00:08:11.792
"I promise, however long
we stay together, we'll have fun."

00:08:13.083 --> 00:08:14.083
"Sudha."

00:08:39.792 --> 00:08:41.875
- Aunty, that's mine!
- Yours?

00:08:41.958 --> 00:08:42.875
Yes.

00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:45.958
If this belongs to you, why is it here?

00:08:46.042 --> 00:08:48.458
I wash my clothes here sometimes.

00:08:48.542 --> 00:08:50.625
You lie so smoothly, don't you?

00:08:50.708 --> 00:08:51.625
Unbelievable!

00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:54.375
How long has she been living here?

00:08:54.458 --> 00:08:56.667
- Who?
- Who?

00:08:57.833 --> 00:08:58.917
Oh…

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.083
Like <i>bhaiya </i>said, she's a friend.

00:09:05.208 --> 00:09:07.792
- A friend's sister.
- Yes!

00:09:17.625 --> 00:09:20.250
Is Chander happy?

00:09:22.042 --> 00:09:23.000
Very happy.

00:09:24.333 --> 00:09:27.333
Every morning,
he wakes up and starts singing.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.167
Chander's special coffee?

00:09:42.333 --> 00:09:43.250
Sure.

00:09:45.083 --> 00:09:48.542
Traveling must be getting on to you,
right? From one place to another.

00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:52.208
I have a flight from Delhi next week.

00:09:52.292 --> 00:09:53.792
Where are you going this time?

00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:56.125
- Bali.
- Wow.

00:09:56.625 --> 00:09:58.125
Ubud Literature Festival.

00:09:58.625 --> 00:10:02.167
And I'm thinking of staying there
until the book release.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.375
Preeti will miss you a lot.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.417
Finding home.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.625
That's my topic of discussion
for the panel there.

00:10:17.458 --> 00:10:18.500
Strange, isn't it?

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:19.958
Why is it strange?

00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:24.833
Maybe I've only come to know
my characters' homes through writing,

00:10:24.917 --> 00:10:26.083
not my own.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.500
But these stories have given you
a lot, Rahil.

00:10:30.083 --> 00:10:33.042
You've made a home in so many hearts
through these stories.

00:10:33.125 --> 00:10:34.792
- Right?
- True.

00:10:37.042 --> 00:10:40.250
But, sometimes, I feel like we waste
so much energy running.

00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:43.833
Sometimes towards something,
and sometimes away from it.

00:10:47.792 --> 00:10:49.500
Do you know what I envy about you?

00:10:49.583 --> 00:10:50.583
- Envy?
- Yes.

00:10:51.125 --> 00:10:54.167
- What?
- That I only write about dreams.

00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:57.750
You built yours and, with coffee
and ginger lemon tea,

00:10:57.833 --> 00:10:59.750
served them to people!

00:11:00.542 --> 00:11:01.500
Amazing.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.958
Thanks.

00:11:05.167 --> 00:11:07.292
I used to run a lot too, Rahil.

00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:09.125
But I stopped

00:11:09.958 --> 00:11:13.875
when I realized that
nothing can top coffee in the mountains.

00:11:15.292 --> 00:11:16.292
I agree.

00:11:18.583 --> 00:11:21.583
You know writers are always looking
for authentic characters.

00:11:22.542 --> 00:11:25.917
In real life, they are rare.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.083
Thanks.

00:11:28.167 --> 00:11:32.042
Chander, I hope you get everything
that you're looking for.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.333
I'm not looking for anything, Rahil.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.250
For me, what I have right now is enough.

00:11:52.042 --> 00:11:54.833
<i>Some travelers set out to see the world,</i>

00:11:56.125 --> 00:11:58.333
<i>while others set out to find a home in it.</i>

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.875
<i>Whenever I meet a new traveler,</i>
<i>I find myself wondering</i>

00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:07.167
<i>which of the two they are.</i>

00:12:18.167 --> 00:12:21.000
The decent, well-bred Chander Sharma

00:12:21.083 --> 00:12:23.500
was found with a girl in his house
early in the morning.

00:12:23.583 --> 00:12:25.750
Caught messing around with a girl!

00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:27.750
Messing around with a girl!

00:12:27.833 --> 00:12:29.833
Nice. What did she say?

00:12:30.375 --> 00:12:31.542
One second.

00:12:33.375 --> 00:12:35.833
- Wait!
- Is that what they said?

00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:41.667
- His Mom's pretty sweet, by the way.
- Really?

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:43.417
The boy is sweet too.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.375
You even like the boy's mom.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.250
Sudha,
what if she talks to your boss lady,

00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:50.583
and finalizes the proposal?

00:12:50.667 --> 00:12:51.750
- So?
- Yeah.

00:12:59.042 --> 00:13:00.000
Sudha?

00:13:01.625 --> 00:13:05.625
I can tell just by looking at you
that you've fallen in love for real.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.417
Who says true love is right for me?

00:13:15.542 --> 00:13:16.708
Doesn't it stress you out?

00:13:16.792 --> 00:13:21.083
What if his mom starts pressuring him
about marriage again?

00:13:22.083 --> 00:13:23.125
So what?

00:13:23.625 --> 00:13:25.875
Chander will do whatever his heart says.

00:13:26.958 --> 00:13:28.917
For me, what I have right now is enough.

00:13:31.417 --> 00:13:32.542
You're useless.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.833
- Let go!
- Hello?

00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:39.917
<i>Hello, Sudha?</i>

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.833
- Yes, sir.
<i>- Regarding your Bombay offer.</i>

00:13:41.917 --> 00:13:43.833
- Yes?
<i>- I know you put it on hold,</i>

00:13:43.917 --> 00:13:45.875
<i>but I spoke to them again today.</i>

00:13:45.958 --> 00:13:49.458
<i>You can specialize in civil disputes,</i>
<i>just like you always wanted.</i>

00:13:49.542 --> 00:13:50.625
Thank you, sir.

00:13:51.125 --> 00:13:53.750
That… I mean, that's…

00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:55.875
That's a huge opportunity, sir.

00:13:56.542 --> 00:13:58.583
If I could just get some time to think…

00:13:58.667 --> 00:14:01.208
<i>I have recommended you strongly.</i>
<i>Don't let me down.</i>

00:14:01.292 --> 00:14:03.375
Yes, thank you, sir. Thank you.

00:14:03.458 --> 00:14:04.458
<i>Okay, bye.</i>

00:14:14.417 --> 00:14:17.250
And if we implement
this plan diligently, sir,

00:14:17.333 --> 00:14:19.708
then I'm expecting a sustainable growth

00:14:19.792 --> 00:14:22.208
of at least five to seven percent
every quarter.

00:14:23.625 --> 00:14:26.917
Chander, implementing this idea
will be very risky.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.792
Sometimes the biggest risk
is not taking any, sir.

00:14:30.958 --> 00:14:32.125
True.

00:14:32.208 --> 00:14:35.417
Just like the professional risk
you're taking by staying in Bhopal.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.042
I know that, sir. We talked about it.

00:14:39.625 --> 00:14:41.625
MOM

00:14:42.958 --> 00:14:44.875
I'm really sorry,
I have to take this call.

00:14:44.958 --> 00:14:46.792
It's my mom calling.
She's visiting Bhopal.

00:14:46.875 --> 00:14:49.208
No problem.
Discuss it with her as well.

00:14:49.833 --> 00:14:50.708
Yes.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.042
Yes, Mom.

00:14:56.792 --> 00:14:58.792
Yes, <i>didi </i>packed lunch for me.

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:02.250
Oh?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.208
Okay, I'll see you
once I'm done with work.

00:15:10.792 --> 00:15:12.417
- Want some more?
- That's enough.

00:15:13.458 --> 00:15:15.375
I ate a lot. It's really good.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:18.083
How's your work going?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.208
It's been busy.

00:15:23.292 --> 00:15:24.750
Do they even give you time off?

00:15:24.833 --> 00:15:27.000
They do, but it's hard right now.

00:15:36.958 --> 00:15:38.000
Check it.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.167
You're not getting time off.

00:15:49.125 --> 00:15:51.250
Nothing is going on with Sudha.

00:15:51.833 --> 00:15:55.208
- What is this, son?
- This… this is just a joke.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.042
- It's a joke.
- A very expensive joke.

00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:01.917
Confirmed booking, honeymoon package!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.833
- How do I explain this to you?
- Oh, please explain.

00:16:03.917 --> 00:16:04.875
Mom.

00:16:05.833 --> 00:16:07.667
Why did you lie about Sudha?

00:16:11.208 --> 00:16:13.083
How could I tell you, Mom?

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:18.458
The girl I once turned down
who I've now fallen…

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.000
Look at your face!

00:16:26.042 --> 00:16:30.417
Now I understand why you've been refusing
to meet other girls every single day.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.292
Silly boy, I've always liked Sudha!

00:16:34.875 --> 00:16:36.708
It's nice that you both gave it time.

00:16:37.333 --> 00:16:39.208
I'll talk to her mom today myself.

00:16:39.292 --> 00:16:41.417
No, no! Wait a minute!

00:16:45.167 --> 00:16:48.625
Mom, it's not what you think.

00:16:48.708 --> 00:16:50.167
Then what is it?

00:16:51.458 --> 00:16:52.417
<i>And what did you say?</i>

00:16:53.417 --> 00:16:54.625
The truth, what else?

00:16:54.708 --> 00:16:56.000
What truth?

00:16:56.083 --> 00:17:00.167
You had a fight with Gargi and came
to stay at my place for a few days.

00:17:00.792 --> 00:17:01.875
And she believed it?

00:17:04.542 --> 00:17:07.625
By the way, how long do you think
your mom will stay?

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.958
The last time she came,
she stayed for almost a month.

00:17:12.042 --> 00:17:13.375
A month?

00:17:13.458 --> 00:17:15.958
What happens to our Andaman tickets now?

00:17:20.583 --> 00:17:23.208
I'm so sorry, Sudha. I'll repay you.

00:17:23.292 --> 00:17:26.000
- Don't be stupid.
- No, I will.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:34.625
It's okay.

00:17:34.708 --> 00:17:37.667
I'll find a loophole for a full refund.

00:17:44.417 --> 00:17:46.458
- Are you upset?
- Of course.

00:17:46.542 --> 00:17:47.792
Come with me tomorrow morning.

00:17:48.958 --> 00:17:51.042
Mala <i>didi </i>will take great care
of your mom.

00:17:51.125 --> 00:17:52.042
Really?

00:17:53.417 --> 00:17:54.667
I'm joking.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:58.250
Mom's going to be after me now.
"If you won't marry Sudha, then…"

00:17:58.958 --> 00:18:01.583
Then go meet some Sita, Gita, or Babita.

00:18:01.667 --> 00:18:05.125
- Oh, stop it!
- No, no, I'm actually being serious.

00:18:05.958 --> 00:18:07.958
Look, that's why your mom is here, right?

00:18:08.042 --> 00:18:10.625
Because her darling son paused
the marriage process.

00:18:10.708 --> 00:18:13.458
And I'm going to Ratlam for a few days.

00:18:13.958 --> 00:18:17.875
So, just meet a couple of girls
for her sake. She'll be happy.

00:18:17.958 --> 00:18:19.750
And then she won't even ask about me.

00:18:20.667 --> 00:18:22.375
Does this seem like a joke to you?

00:18:24.958 --> 00:18:26.833
And what if I actually like someone?

00:18:31.583 --> 00:18:34.167
I've always made five-year plans
for my life.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.792
From now till 2023.

00:18:35.875 --> 00:18:38.292
First comes the engagement,
then the wedding,

00:18:38.375 --> 00:18:41.750
then a house, and finally a baby.

00:18:41.833 --> 00:18:44.875
My cousin's wedding was big and beautiful.

00:18:44.958 --> 00:18:48.042
So, in my opinion,
big weddings are always better.

00:18:48.125 --> 00:18:49.875
What's your opinion on this?

00:18:50.875 --> 00:18:53.500
<i>Give me a status update.</i>
<i>How was Rinku?</i>

00:18:54.292 --> 00:18:55.750
<i>Send help, please.</i>

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.292
<i>Please, have something.</i>

00:18:59.375 --> 00:19:02.083
Mom has put me on a diet.

00:19:02.167 --> 00:19:03.458
<i>Makhana?</i>

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.167
<i>How are the samosas?</i>

00:19:07.917 --> 00:19:10.542
<i>Poor thing is on a diet.</i>
<i>But she's very sweet.</i>

00:19:13.125 --> 00:19:16.083
<i>The number you have dialled</i>
<i>is currently busy.</i>

00:19:16.167 --> 00:19:18.833
<i>- Please call again later.</i>
<i>- I'll call you later.</i>

00:19:18.917 --> 00:19:20.958
<i>If you like her so much, say yes!</i>

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.458
- What is Sudha saying?
- Mom…

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:43.000
No. Nothing. We're just talking.

00:19:45.292 --> 00:19:48.167
I saw it clearly on your face
the very first day.

00:19:50.542 --> 00:19:52.083
Why did you meet the other girls?

00:19:52.167 --> 00:19:54.208
Just to make me happy?

00:19:55.042 --> 00:19:56.125
Silly!

00:19:59.208 --> 00:20:02.542
If you like her so much,
then what's the problem?

00:20:08.583 --> 00:20:11.292
She doesn't want to get married.

00:20:13.125 --> 00:20:14.292
Problem solved.

00:20:14.917 --> 00:20:18.167
We can have the <i>Roka </i>now, and you
can get married a year or two later.

00:20:23.625 --> 00:20:24.875
Did you know?

00:20:25.708 --> 00:20:26.875
From the start.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.500
Why doesn't she want to get married?

00:20:35.583 --> 00:20:37.167
Mom, she doesn't have a father.

00:20:39.125 --> 00:20:41.750
Her mom lives by herself
in a joint family system.

00:20:41.833 --> 00:20:44.167
She wants to take care of her.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:45.750
That's her priority.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:48.750
And…

00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:55.292
she has seen up close everything
society expects from women after marriage.

00:20:55.833 --> 00:20:59.000
Through her mom
and other women in her family.

00:21:00.333 --> 00:21:02.125
She sees it every day in court as well.

00:21:04.917 --> 00:21:05.875
And?

00:21:08.875 --> 00:21:11.250
And she wants to travel the world

00:21:11.333 --> 00:21:13.333
and open her own law firm.

00:21:15.375 --> 00:21:17.125
- And?
- What else?

00:21:18.375 --> 00:21:21.333
She wants to fulfil all
of her dreams, Mom.

00:21:22.417 --> 00:21:25.292
And she can't do all that
while being with you?

00:21:29.417 --> 00:21:31.417
Chander, you're not the kind of person

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:34.083
who would have unfair expectations
of his partner,

00:21:34.708 --> 00:21:36.708
or stand in the way of her dreams.

00:21:37.333 --> 00:21:39.000
Nor are we those kinds of people.

00:21:40.042 --> 00:21:44.917
Give Sudha some time to understand me,
your father, and our family.

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:47.583
Who knows, she might change her mind.

00:21:49.333 --> 00:21:51.500
If you get to know Sudha a little better,

00:21:52.167 --> 00:21:53.958
could your mind change?

00:22:03.625 --> 00:22:05.833
How long will you wait for her?

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:09.583
Two years? Five years?

00:22:10.625 --> 00:22:11.708
I don't know.

00:22:13.417 --> 00:22:14.625
No, that's good.

00:22:15.625 --> 00:22:19.208
It's good that she wants to take care
of her mother, and she should.

00:22:19.708 --> 00:22:22.625
She wants to build a career for herself,
and of course, she should.

00:22:22.708 --> 00:22:25.083
She wants to travel the world,
and she should.

00:22:25.708 --> 00:22:30.125
Actually, she wants to do everything
that's important to her in her life.

00:22:30.625 --> 00:22:32.708
She just doesn't want to marry you.

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:40.917
No… No, it's not like that, Mom.

00:22:41.958 --> 00:22:44.417
She just doesn't
want to get married right now.

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:47.792
Yeah.

00:22:49.417 --> 00:22:51.250
Are you trying to convince me or yourself?

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:00.042
Chander, relationships only work
when both sides are willing to compromise.

00:23:00.917 --> 00:23:04.958
Does Sudha know what
you're compromising in this relationship?

00:23:05.042 --> 00:23:08.917
Have you ever told her
what you sacrifice by being with her?

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:17.167
Okay, suppose
she says yes to marriage tomorrow.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:18.833
You'd marry her, right?

00:23:18.917 --> 00:23:21.167
Because as far as I know my son,

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:24.875
he has always dreamed of
having a home, a family, and kids.

00:23:34.125 --> 00:23:36.750
I've booked my return ticket for tomorrow.
I'm leaving in the morning.

00:23:36.833 --> 00:23:38.542
What? Why?

00:23:50.458 --> 00:23:51.500
And, Chander…

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:55.417
this has happened to you before.

00:23:58.625 --> 00:23:59.625
Not again.

00:26:36.875 --> 00:26:38.875
Subtitle translation by: Neha Nair


